WEBVTT

00:00:03.003 --> 00:00:04.595
No! Make them stop!

00:00:04.671 --> 00:00:05.603
Anything?

00:00:05.672 --> 00:00:06.696
Nothing of relevance.

00:00:06.773 --> 00:00:08.604
His neural pathways
are still fluctuating.

00:00:08.675 --> 00:00:10.233
Doc...

00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:11.607
Can't you do something?

00:00:11.678 --> 00:00:12.610
Look how much he's suffering.

00:00:12.679 --> 00:00:14.112
If I sedate him,
we could lose any chance

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:15.772
of making contact
with the aliens.

00:00:15.849 --> 00:00:16.781
Get them out!

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:18.147
Commander, can you hear me?

00:00:18.218 --> 00:00:20.778
Focus on the sound of my voice.

00:00:20.854 --> 00:00:22.082
I can't understand them,

00:00:22.155 --> 00:00:23.622
but they won't stop talking!

00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:24.622
What are they saying?

00:00:24.691 --> 00:00:26.556
I don't know!

00:00:26.626 --> 00:00:28.321
Make them stop! Please!

00:00:29.362 --> 00:00:30.761
Janeway to Sick Bay.

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:32.627
Any progress, Doctor?

00:00:32.699 --> 00:00:33.631
It's not going well.

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:35.964
Our "Ambassador"
is still delusional.

00:00:36.102 --> 00:00:37.967
We're running out of time.

00:00:39.039 --> 00:00:41.064
The graviton shear
is buckling the hull.

00:00:41.141 --> 00:00:43.234
If we don't find a way
out of chaotic space soon,

00:00:43.309 --> 00:00:44.776
we're going to die here.

00:02:41.361 --> 00:02:43.829
Chief Medical Officer's Log,
supplemental.

00:02:43.897 --> 00:02:45.524
Despite my efforts,

00:02:45.598 --> 00:02:48.829
Chakotay's condition
continues to deteriorate.

00:02:49.869 --> 00:02:51.200
Doctor!

00:02:54.574 --> 00:02:56.098
Yes, Commander?

00:02:56.176 --> 00:02:57.871
I'm tired.
I want to sleep.

00:02:57.944 --> 00:02:59.536
If you lose consciousness,

00:02:59.612 --> 00:03:02.308
it could sever your link
with the aliens.

00:03:02.382 --> 00:03:03.314
Aliens?

00:03:03.383 --> 00:03:05.112
The ones who live in this place.

00:03:05.185 --> 00:03:06.243
We're trapped here.

00:03:06.319 --> 00:03:07.581
They may know a way out.

00:03:07.654 --> 00:03:09.588
It's urgent
that you speak with them.

00:03:09.656 --> 00:03:11.681
But I don't understand
what they're saying.

00:03:11.758 --> 00:03:13.385
I can try
to help you understand.

00:03:13.459 --> 00:03:15.324
I'm going to end up
like my grandfather...

00:03:15.395 --> 00:03:16.327
a crazy old man.

00:03:16.396 --> 00:03:18.728
No. You're not crazy.
I believe the aliens

00:03:18.798 --> 00:03:20.925
are reconfiguring
your neural pathways,

00:03:21.067 --> 00:03:23.900
so they can
communicate with you.

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:25.437
Do you remember the day

00:03:25.505 --> 00:03:27.769
you were injured
on the holodeck?

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:29.432
In the boxing simulation?

00:03:29.509 --> 00:03:33.377
Yes. You were knocked down,
remember?

00:03:33.446 --> 00:03:35.141
I was injured.

00:03:35.215 --> 00:03:36.910
I came to see you.

00:03:36.983 --> 00:03:38.348
We had an argument.

00:03:38.418 --> 00:03:40.045
That's right.

00:03:40.119 --> 00:03:43.088
Try to remember more
about the holodeck.

00:03:43.156 --> 00:03:45.954
I was sparring
with a Terrellian...

00:03:46.025 --> 00:03:47.890
and Boothby was there.

00:03:47.961 --> 00:03:50.759
He used to train me
when I was a cadet.

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:52.491
Keep going.

00:03:52.565 --> 00:03:55.557
What round was it?

00:03:55.635 --> 00:03:58.695
Three. Round Three.

00:03:58.771 --> 00:04:00.602
The fight was going badly.

00:04:00.673 --> 00:04:02.766
I was avoiding my opponent.

00:04:22.462 --> 00:04:24.362
Stay away from the ropes, son.

00:04:26.032 --> 00:04:27.294
That's it, that's it.

00:04:35.041 --> 00:04:37.635
End Round Three.

00:04:39.078 --> 00:04:40.511
That wasn't so bad.

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:42.343
It was terrible.

00:04:42.415 --> 00:04:43.677
Am I missing something?

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:45.479
He barely landed a glove on me.

00:04:45.551 --> 00:04:46.882
Mm-hmm.
Give him time.

00:04:46.953 --> 00:04:48.511
You're not reading him.

00:04:48.588 --> 00:04:50.556
You think he's slow and stupid.

00:04:50.623 --> 00:04:51.851
I know better.

00:04:51.924 --> 00:04:55.792
In fact, I know his kind
in my bones. Literally.

00:04:55.862 --> 00:04:58.057
I can count the fractures,
if you'd like.

00:04:58.131 --> 00:04:59.063
He's not landing any punches.

00:04:59.132 --> 00:05:00.064
That's the problem.

00:05:00.133 --> 00:05:01.327
You're not letting him.

00:05:01.401 --> 00:05:02.868
Have I got this sport all wrong?

00:05:02.935 --> 00:05:05.403
Boxing is more
about taking the shots

00:05:05.471 --> 00:05:06.665
than dishing them out.

00:05:06.739 --> 00:05:09.299
You shouldn't be dancing
away from this fella.

00:05:09.375 --> 00:05:11.309
Let him punch himself
out a little.

00:05:11.377 --> 00:05:13.277
It all comes down to the heart.

00:05:13.346 --> 00:05:15.473
Do you have the heart
for this?

00:05:15.548 --> 00:05:18.676
That's the contest...
it's not against him.

00:05:18.751 --> 00:05:23.586
It's against your own natural
human desire not to get hurt.

00:05:23.656 --> 00:05:25.817
That's the real fight.

00:05:25.892 --> 00:05:27.587
Begin Round Four.

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:28.718
Go.

00:05:28.795 --> 00:05:30.854
Go, go, go.

00:05:35.034 --> 00:05:36.023
Stay with him.

00:05:45.311 --> 00:05:47.779
Too close. Come on,
come on. Break it up.

00:05:50.116 --> 00:05:51.549
Thataboy.
Keep him busy.

00:06:06.466 --> 00:06:08.457
Cover up!

00:06:28.388 --> 00:06:30.185
How many?

00:06:37.029 --> 00:06:39.088
Three.

00:06:39.165 --> 00:06:40.632
Good guess.

00:06:42.168 --> 00:06:44.728
I've got a good mind to
use a needle and thread

00:06:44.804 --> 00:06:46.795
add a little authenticity
to your fun.

00:06:46.873 --> 00:06:48.170
Be my guest.

00:06:48.241 --> 00:06:51.472
You'd like that...
a manly scar above your eye.

00:06:51.544 --> 00:06:53.944
"Chakotay...
the Maquis Mauler."

00:06:54.080 --> 00:06:56.071
Pointless violence.

00:06:56.149 --> 00:06:58.617
That program shouldn't
even be in our database.

00:06:58.684 --> 00:07:00.914
There's nothing like
a good fight, Doctor.

00:07:00.987 --> 00:07:04.218
I was there when Price Jones
went 23 rounds with Gul Tulet.

00:07:04.290 --> 00:07:06.155
"The Knockout
in the Neutral Zone."

00:07:06.225 --> 00:07:07.453
Best match I ever saw.

00:07:07.527 --> 00:07:08.459
Really?

00:07:08.528 --> 00:07:10.325
Most blood spilled?

00:07:10.396 --> 00:07:12.057
Or did Price Jones

00:07:12.131 --> 00:07:15.328
drive Gul Tulet's nasal bone
up into his brain?

00:07:16.736 --> 00:07:17.896
You've got the wrong idea.

00:07:18.004 --> 00:07:19.232
The idea is simple enough.

00:07:19.305 --> 00:07:21.068
Do enough damage
to your opponent

00:07:21.140 --> 00:07:22.630
to render him unconscious.

00:07:23.709 --> 00:07:26.371
How's the headache?

00:07:26.446 --> 00:07:27.913
It hurts.

00:07:28.047 --> 00:07:31.448
Edema beneath the anterior fossa
of the cranium...

00:07:31.517 --> 00:07:33.382
hairline fracture
of the septum...

00:07:36.722 --> 00:07:38.417
I saw something strange.

00:07:38.491 --> 00:07:39.685
I'll bet you did.

00:07:39.759 --> 00:07:41.090
No, before I got hit.

00:07:42.161 --> 00:07:43.594
What do you mean?

00:07:43.663 --> 00:07:46.860
I looked over at Boothby...

00:07:46.933 --> 00:07:49.265
He yelled at me...

00:07:49.335 --> 00:07:51.769
I turned back...

00:07:51.838 --> 00:07:53.931
Then the ring got distorted.

00:07:54.073 --> 00:07:55.802
An hallucination.

00:07:55.875 --> 00:07:57.843
You probably had
some pressure building up

00:07:57.910 --> 00:07:59.935
along the optic nerves
from a previous blow.

00:08:00.079 --> 00:08:02.343
No. I was keeping away
from him the whole fight.

00:08:02.415 --> 00:08:03.382
He never touched me.

00:08:03.449 --> 00:08:06.111
Hmm.
A number of the ganglia

00:08:06.185 --> 00:08:09.211
in your visual cortex
are hyperactive.

00:08:09.288 --> 00:08:11.119
Your opponent
wasn't firing on you

00:08:11.190 --> 00:08:12.817
with an energy weapon, was he?

00:08:12.892 --> 00:08:16.055
Just his gloves.

00:08:16.128 --> 00:08:17.652
Chakotay to the Bridge.

00:08:17.730 --> 00:08:18.890
On my way.

00:08:18.965 --> 00:08:20.865
I want you back in here
for some tests...

00:08:20.933 --> 00:08:22.696
unless you want
to be seeing things

00:08:22.768 --> 00:08:23.792
on a regular basis.

00:08:30.476 --> 00:08:31.909
It's changed course again...

00:08:31.978 --> 00:08:33.673
20,000 kilometers
off starboard.

00:08:38.184 --> 00:08:39.549
Ion storm?

00:08:39.619 --> 00:08:40.711
Not exactly.

00:08:40.786 --> 00:08:42.083
It's two light-years across,

00:08:42.154 --> 00:08:44.088
emits enough energy
for a dozen stars.

00:08:44.156 --> 00:08:46.386
It doesn't match any phenomenon
in our database,

00:08:46.459 --> 00:08:48.723
and it won't sit still.

00:08:50.663 --> 00:08:53.632
Okay. 11,000 kilometers
off the port bow.

00:08:55.134 --> 00:08:56.567
We are too close.

00:08:56.636 --> 00:08:58.297
I'm backing us off.

00:08:58.371 --> 00:09:00.931
The phenomenon has been shifting
positions every few minutes.

00:09:01.073 --> 00:09:03.667
Nothing so massive
could move that fast.

00:09:07.647 --> 00:09:08.579
Full reverse.

00:09:08.648 --> 00:09:09.615
Maximum shields.

00:09:23.729 --> 00:09:25.959
Full stop.

00:09:34.674 --> 00:09:37.609
Anybody want to tell me
where we are?

00:09:37.677 --> 00:09:41.670
We appear to be
inside the disturbance.

00:09:41.747 --> 00:09:43.874
I'm picking up
a lot of raw data...

00:09:43.950 --> 00:09:45.713
subspace flux, graviton waves.

00:09:45.785 --> 00:09:47.218
Sensors must be confused.

00:09:47.286 --> 00:09:49.379
The readings are shifting
around so much, I can't make

00:09:49.455 --> 00:09:50.649
heads or tails
of what's out there.

00:09:50.723 --> 00:09:52.350
Captain, this is Seven of Nine.

00:09:52.425 --> 00:09:54.450
Please report
to Astrometrics at once.

00:09:56.228 --> 00:09:59.425
The Borg have been aware of
this phenomenon for many years.

00:09:59.498 --> 00:10:01.523
It's a zone
where the laws of physics

00:10:01.601 --> 00:10:04.502
are in a state of
flux..."chaotic space."

00:10:04.570 --> 00:10:06.629
Why didn't sensors
warn us in time?

00:10:06.706 --> 00:10:09.937
Chaotic space appears randomly
and unexpectedly.

00:10:10.009 --> 00:10:13.240
The Borg have observed it
throughout the galaxy.

00:10:13.312 --> 00:10:14.870
Then why hasn't
a Federation starship

00:10:14.947 --> 00:10:16.209
encountered anything like this?

00:10:16.282 --> 00:10:18.045
No doubt some have.

00:10:18.117 --> 00:10:19.914
Think of all
the Starfleet vessels

00:10:19.986 --> 00:10:22.580
that disappeared under
mysterious circumstances.

00:10:22.655 --> 00:10:24.350
Borg vessels
are more advanced,

00:10:24.423 --> 00:10:27.586
but only one cube has survived
an encounter with chaotic space.

00:10:27.660 --> 00:10:29.127
Those aren't good odds.

00:10:29.195 --> 00:10:31.595
If the physical constants
are shifting,

00:10:31.664 --> 00:10:33.154
our sensors can't function.

00:10:33.232 --> 00:10:34.358
The problem is here.

00:10:34.433 --> 00:10:36.765
Changes in the gravitational
coefficient

00:10:36.836 --> 00:10:39.703
will cause sudden shear
forces against our hull.

00:10:39.772 --> 00:10:41.672
Shields will protect us,
but only for a time.

00:10:41.741 --> 00:10:42.867
How much time?

00:10:42.942 --> 00:10:44.705
Unknown.

00:10:44.777 --> 00:10:46.802
We've got to recalibrate
the sensors...

00:10:46.879 --> 00:10:48.369
redesign them if necessary.

00:10:48.447 --> 00:10:50.142
Otherwise,
we're flying blind.

00:10:50.216 --> 00:10:51.240
Let's get to work.

00:11:14.006 --> 00:11:17.134
Begin Round One.

00:11:17.209 --> 00:11:20.144
Computer, did you say something?

00:11:20.212 --> 00:11:21.873
Negative.

00:11:40.666 --> 00:11:41.963
Pick 'em up, son.

00:11:42.068 --> 00:11:44.901
It's the fight
you've been waiting for.

00:11:47.006 --> 00:11:50.567
Begin Round One.

00:11:51.811 --> 00:11:54.143
Bridge to Commander Chakotay.

00:11:54.213 --> 00:11:56.408
Go ahead, Tuvok.

00:11:56.482 --> 00:11:58.712
Please report to the Bridge.

00:11:58.784 --> 00:12:00.183
On my way.

00:12:11.497 --> 00:12:14.261
Graviton wave displacement
says we're moving at warp 6.

00:12:14.333 --> 00:12:17.530
Subspace sensors show
we're standing still.

00:12:17.603 --> 00:12:19.503
We can't be that far
from where we entered.

00:12:19.572 --> 00:12:20.937
Maybe we should
just set a course,

00:12:21.073 --> 00:12:22.631
go to impulse
and see what happens.

00:12:22.708 --> 00:12:24.039
What would most likely happen

00:12:24.110 --> 00:12:26.101
is a collision with
an asteroid field or a star.

00:12:26.178 --> 00:12:28.271
That'd be better
than just sitting here...

00:12:28.347 --> 00:12:29.609
Report.

00:12:29.682 --> 00:12:32.116
Torsional shear has
increased by 200 percent.

00:12:32.184 --> 00:12:33.276
Shields?

00:12:33.352 --> 00:12:34.319
Holding.

00:12:36.689 --> 00:12:38.179
Like I was saying,

00:12:38.257 --> 00:12:39.849
better than just
sitting here waiting

00:12:39.925 --> 00:12:40.892
for our hull to breach.

00:12:40.960 --> 00:12:42.188
Perhaps we could drop

00:12:42.261 --> 00:12:44.229
a series of beacons
to help us navigate.

00:12:44.296 --> 00:12:45.558
Now that's an idea.

00:12:47.166 --> 00:12:49.498
Did you hear something?

00:12:49.568 --> 00:12:51.627
I heard nothing unusual.

00:12:51.704 --> 00:12:54.229
I didn't hear anything.

00:12:54.306 --> 00:12:57.571
Begin Round One.

00:12:57.643 --> 00:13:00.134
I'll plot a course
and we'll take it slow.

00:13:00.212 --> 00:13:01.645
What do you think, Chakotay?

00:13:01.714 --> 00:13:05.115
The challenger... Chakotay!

00:13:05.184 --> 00:13:06.617
Don't you hear that?

00:13:06.685 --> 00:13:08.243
Hear what?

00:13:11.323 --> 00:13:13.382
Look.

00:13:15.461 --> 00:13:16.519
Commander?

00:13:19.398 --> 00:13:22.026
Are you all right?

00:13:22.101 --> 00:13:23.932
Put on the gloves, son.

00:13:24.003 --> 00:13:25.368
I'm not ready.

00:13:25.437 --> 00:13:27.371
Commander.

00:13:27.439 --> 00:13:31.170
In this corner,
wearing the red trunks...

00:13:31.243 --> 00:13:32.608
Begin Round One.

00:13:34.413 --> 00:13:37.211
Bridge to Sick Bay.
We've got a medical emergency.

00:13:54.533 --> 00:13:55.966
Mm-hmm.

00:13:56.068 --> 00:13:58.400
Let's go to 880 hertz.

00:14:02.007 --> 00:14:03.269
Music lessons?

00:14:03.342 --> 00:14:05.276
Pretty soon
we'll be singing duets.

00:14:05.344 --> 00:14:07.244
I'm checking to see
if there's been any damage

00:14:07.313 --> 00:14:09.474
to the auditory nerves...
nothing so far.

00:14:09.548 --> 00:14:11.641
His vision checks out as well.

00:14:11.717 --> 00:14:14.117
I'm afraid
the source of the trouble

00:14:14.186 --> 00:14:16.586
may be a little... deeper.

00:14:16.655 --> 00:14:18.020
The family curse.

00:14:18.090 --> 00:14:19.079
What do you mean?

00:14:19.158 --> 00:14:20.887
Chakotay has the genetic marker

00:14:20.960 --> 00:14:23.326
for a cognitive disorder...
sensory tremens.

00:14:23.395 --> 00:14:26.762
The primary symptoms are visual
and auditory hallucinations.

00:14:26.832 --> 00:14:28.891
My family doctor
suppressed the gene

00:14:28.968 --> 00:14:30.333
before I was even born,

00:14:30.402 --> 00:14:33.428
so I never had to go through
what the others did...

00:14:33.505 --> 00:14:34.767
like my grandfather.

00:14:34.840 --> 00:14:37.308
For some reason,
the gene's been switched on.

00:14:37.376 --> 00:14:39.207
I'm not saying for certain
that's why Chakotay thought

00:14:39.278 --> 00:14:40.768
he was getting ready
for a prizefight,

00:14:40.846 --> 00:14:42.814
but it's a good bet;
the holodeck boxing

00:14:42.882 --> 00:14:44.907
simulation was fresh
in his memory.

00:14:44.984 --> 00:14:47.145
A few misfiring neurons
did the rest.

00:14:47.219 --> 00:14:49.187
This chaotic space
we've entered...

00:14:49.255 --> 00:14:51.189
could it be stimulating
the gene?

00:14:51.257 --> 00:14:53.384
Possibly. The only way
to make certain

00:14:53.459 --> 00:14:55.290
would be to get the ship
out of here.

00:14:55.361 --> 00:14:57.488
In the meantime,
the Commander will have

00:14:57.563 --> 00:14:58.962
to stay in Sick Bay.

00:15:00.966 --> 00:15:04.402
Tuvok tells me
you've got a mean left jab.

00:15:05.971 --> 00:15:08.439
Never spar with a Vulcan.

00:15:09.875 --> 00:15:11.740
How are you doing?

00:15:12.978 --> 00:15:14.445
I'm all right.

00:15:18.484 --> 00:15:20.918
When I was a boy...

00:15:20.986 --> 00:15:24.422
my grandfather
started seeing things

00:15:24.490 --> 00:15:26.424
nobody else could see...

00:15:26.492 --> 00:15:29.256
hearing what nobody else
could hear.

00:15:29.328 --> 00:15:31.228
He refused treatment.

00:15:32.831 --> 00:15:37.530
A couple of hyposprays a day,
that's all he would have needed.

00:15:37.603 --> 00:15:39.867
But he was stubborn.

00:15:39.939 --> 00:15:43.136
He said
his spirit was in pain...

00:15:43.208 --> 00:15:44.937
but that the wound...

00:15:45.010 --> 00:15:47.808
must be honored.

00:15:52.851 --> 00:15:54.478
Crazy old man.

00:15:59.558 --> 00:16:01.048
Ready, Captain.

00:16:01.126 --> 00:16:02.388
Janeway to Seven.

00:16:02.461 --> 00:16:04.224
Bring the grid back on line.

00:16:04.296 --> 00:16:05.729
Stand by.

00:16:05.798 --> 00:16:07.857
We've got sensors.

00:16:07.933 --> 00:16:10.629
I'm scanning
to 100,000 kilometers...

00:16:10.703 --> 00:16:12.432
700,000.

00:16:12.504 --> 00:16:16.099
Sensors are stable
to one million kilometers.

00:16:16.175 --> 00:16:17.506
We won't be able
to scan any further.

00:16:17.576 --> 00:16:19.567
Are you picking up
anything at that range?

00:16:19.645 --> 00:16:22.375
No planets, no asteroid fields,
no sinkholes.

00:16:22.448 --> 00:16:24.541
Good enough for me.

00:16:24.616 --> 00:16:26.174
Set a course dead ahead
one-quarter impulse.

00:16:31.256 --> 00:16:32.587
Sensor status?

00:16:32.658 --> 00:16:34.819
Continuing to function.

00:16:34.893 --> 00:16:36.758
Still nothing ahead.

00:16:36.829 --> 00:16:38.091
Good.

00:16:38.163 --> 00:16:39.653
Let's increase our speed.

00:16:39.732 --> 00:16:41.597
Mr. Paris, go to half impulse.

00:16:41.667 --> 00:16:42.929
Wait.

00:16:43.002 --> 00:16:44.902
It's a ship.

00:16:44.970 --> 00:16:46.232
Warp capable.

00:16:46.305 --> 00:16:48.398
It's adrift,
and the outer hull is damaged.

00:16:48.474 --> 00:16:50.408
No life-signs.

00:16:52.511 --> 00:16:54.604
Let's take a closer look.

00:16:54.680 --> 00:16:56.511
Computer, let's hear that again.

00:16:56.582 --> 00:16:58.812
Why won't you answer?

00:16:58.884 --> 00:17:02.285
Did you give up on me
for being so late?

00:17:02.354 --> 00:17:03.480
Not my fault.

00:17:04.623 --> 00:17:06.250
We got lost in here.

00:17:06.325 --> 00:17:09.692
Why do the stars
make such a noise?

00:17:09.762 --> 00:17:11.423
Let me sleep.

00:17:11.497 --> 00:17:12.691
I don't understand them.

00:17:12.765 --> 00:17:14.289
I don't want to talk to them.

00:17:14.366 --> 00:17:16.266
I just want to go home.

00:17:19.471 --> 00:17:21.405
That was the final
distress call.

00:17:21.473 --> 00:17:23.634
According to the vessel's
medical records,

00:17:23.709 --> 00:17:25.609
the Captain and one
of his engineers

00:17:25.677 --> 00:17:28.407
started hallucinating
after they entered this space.

00:17:28.480 --> 00:17:31.574
The physician on board
never found a way to treat them.

00:17:31.650 --> 00:17:33.584
How long were
they stranded here?

00:17:33.652 --> 00:17:35.085
Almost a year.

00:17:35.154 --> 00:17:37.452
Eventually, their systems
were compromised.

00:17:37.523 --> 00:17:38.922
They died of exposure.

00:17:38.991 --> 00:17:41.323
The sensors on that ship
are more advanced than ours

00:17:41.393 --> 00:17:43.293
and they couldn't find
a way out.

00:17:43.362 --> 00:17:44.761
Let's hold our position

00:17:44.830 --> 00:17:47.594
till we have a better idea
of what we're up against.

00:17:47.666 --> 00:17:49.531
It looks like that's
what they did.

00:17:49.601 --> 00:17:51.694
And along the way,
a couple of them

00:17:51.770 --> 00:17:53.931
started sounding
just like Chakotay.

00:17:54.006 --> 00:17:56.304
I can't believe
that's a coincidence.

00:17:56.375 --> 00:17:57.865
Then why hasn't anyone
else been affected?

00:17:57.943 --> 00:17:59.274
That's a question
I can't answer.

00:17:59.344 --> 00:18:00.811
Not yet.

00:18:00.879 --> 00:18:03.814
Request permission to beam
their Captain's body on board.

00:18:03.882 --> 00:18:05.406
I'd like to perform an autopsy.

00:18:05.484 --> 00:18:07.884
Granted. Pull the sensor
technology off that ship.

00:18:07.986 --> 00:18:09.317
Use it to enhance ours.

00:18:09.388 --> 00:18:11.754
We're going to need
all the help we can get.

00:18:16.728 --> 00:18:17.888
I made a deep scan

00:18:17.996 --> 00:18:21.022
of the alien's brain tissue
and sensory organs.

00:18:21.100 --> 00:18:24.831
The optic and auditory neurons
have been partially stripped

00:18:24.903 --> 00:18:27.167
of their normal
protein insulation.

00:18:27.239 --> 00:18:28.570
The result...

00:18:28.640 --> 00:18:30.437
auditory and visual
hallucinations.

00:18:30.509 --> 00:18:33.137
The same symptoms as Chakotay
but a different cause.

00:18:33.212 --> 00:18:35.305
Exactly. In this case,
the gene responsible

00:18:35.380 --> 00:18:38.042
for producing protein insulation
was shut down.

00:18:38.117 --> 00:18:39.175
By what?

00:18:39.251 --> 00:18:41.845
There might be something
in chaotic space

00:18:41.920 --> 00:18:44.616
that reacts with DNA...
alters it.

00:18:44.690 --> 00:18:47.659
But why it targeted him
specifically and now you,

00:18:47.726 --> 00:18:48.750
I can't say.

00:18:48.827 --> 00:18:50.522
Is there a treatment?

00:18:50.596 --> 00:18:52.621
I can control
the hallucinations using

00:18:52.698 --> 00:18:56.429
a neural suppressant,
but, unless I can find

00:18:56.502 --> 00:18:58.436
a way to deactivate
that gene of yours...

00:18:58.504 --> 00:19:00.404
I need to go
on a vision quest. Captain?

00:19:00.472 --> 00:19:02.702
That's not the best
idea right now.

00:19:02.774 --> 00:19:06.210
A vision quest taps directly
into your frontal cortex.

00:19:06.278 --> 00:19:08.007
It could agitate your mind.

00:19:08.080 --> 00:19:09.342
Or help me control it.

00:19:11.283 --> 00:19:12.773
Permission granted.

00:19:14.286 --> 00:19:15.617
Very well.

00:19:15.687 --> 00:19:18.121
I will ask you to wear
a cortical monitor.

00:19:20.959 --> 00:19:23.757
It will help me keep
track of your vital signs.

00:19:37.142 --> 00:19:40.077
Ah-koo-chee-moya.

00:19:40.145 --> 00:19:43.740
I am far from the sacred places
of my grandfathers.

00:19:43.815 --> 00:19:46.909
I am far from the bones
of my people,

00:19:46.985 --> 00:19:50.751
but perhaps there is a powerful
being who will embrace me

00:19:50.822 --> 00:19:54.451
and give me the answers I seek.

00:20:03.869 --> 00:20:07.100
Grandfather,
what are you doing here?

00:20:07.172 --> 00:20:08.833
I, uh...

00:20:08.907 --> 00:20:11.933
seem to be... lost.

00:20:12.077 --> 00:20:13.374
Just a little lost.

00:20:13.445 --> 00:20:15.777
You didn't take your medicine
this morning.

00:20:15.847 --> 00:20:17.644
Which medicine are
you talking about?

00:20:17.716 --> 00:20:18.648
There are many medicines.

00:20:18.717 --> 00:20:20.207
The one the hospital gave us.

00:20:20.285 --> 00:20:22.651
Oh, that one.

00:20:22.721 --> 00:20:25.246
Where are you going?

00:20:25.324 --> 00:20:27.884
My spirit doesn't
want that medicine.

00:20:27.960 --> 00:20:29.757
I don't care
what your spirit wants.

00:20:29.828 --> 00:20:31.455
You're going to take it.

00:20:31.530 --> 00:20:33.361
I don't think so.

00:20:33.432 --> 00:20:35.423
Come with me back to the house.

00:20:35.500 --> 00:20:37.297
Now why would
I want to do that?

00:20:37.369 --> 00:20:38.893
It's better where I'm going.

00:20:38.971 --> 00:20:41.565
It's more interesting.

00:20:44.176 --> 00:20:45.666
Where are you going?

00:20:45.744 --> 00:20:49.680
To the place
where my spirit lives.

00:21:01.493 --> 00:21:03.154
Grandfather!

00:21:05.998 --> 00:21:08.398
Where are you?

00:21:08.467 --> 00:21:10.094
Answer me!

00:21:11.503 --> 00:21:13.767
Begin Round One.

00:21:39.031 --> 00:21:41.158
Begin Round One.

00:21:45.037 --> 00:21:46.129
The aliens.

00:21:46.204 --> 00:21:48.968
They were there, watching me.

00:21:49.074 --> 00:21:50.701
Inside your vision quest?

00:21:50.776 --> 00:21:52.744
They were trying
to tell me something.

00:21:52.811 --> 00:21:53.971
What was it?

00:21:54.112 --> 00:21:55.739
I don't know.

00:21:55.814 --> 00:21:57.372
Are they with you now?

00:21:57.449 --> 00:21:58.381
Can you hear them?

00:21:58.450 --> 00:21:59.382
Yes.

00:21:59.451 --> 00:22:00.383
Let them speak to you.

00:22:00.452 --> 00:22:02.386
No!
They'll make me go crazy.

00:22:02.454 --> 00:22:03.386
You're not going crazy.

00:22:03.455 --> 00:22:04.615
They're doing this for a reason.

00:22:04.690 --> 00:22:05.714
You've got to trust them.

00:22:07.492 --> 00:22:09.619
Stop fighting.

00:22:09.695 --> 00:22:11.219
Open your mind.

00:22:11.296 --> 00:22:12.763
Let go.

00:22:14.166 --> 00:22:15.633
Listen.

00:22:18.503 --> 00:22:22.667
Chaotic space...
intersects ours...

00:22:22.741 --> 00:22:25.904
at the 18th
dimensional gradient.

00:22:25.977 --> 00:22:28.411
Voyager entered through...

00:22:32.050 --> 00:22:33.677
a trimetric fracture.

00:22:33.752 --> 00:22:35.743
Trimetric fracture?

00:22:35.821 --> 00:22:38.585
We must escape,
or we'll be destroyed.

00:22:38.657 --> 00:22:40.181
How do we escape?

00:22:40.258 --> 00:22:42.590
We've got to alter
our warp field.

00:22:42.661 --> 00:22:43.958
In what way?

00:22:44.096 --> 00:22:46.462
Rentrillic trajectory.

00:22:46.531 --> 00:22:48.431
Rentrillic?

00:22:49.501 --> 00:22:50.729
It doesn't make any sense.

00:22:50.802 --> 00:22:51.860
I can't understand it.

00:22:51.937 --> 00:22:53.268
I'm scared I'm losing my mind!

00:22:53.338 --> 00:22:54.168
Try to focus.

00:22:55.240 --> 00:22:56.400
It's too much!

00:22:56.475 --> 00:22:57.840
I can't! It's too much!

00:22:57.909 --> 00:22:58.637
Chakotay!

00:22:59.711 --> 00:23:01.269
Get them out!

00:23:07.552 --> 00:23:08.917
First contact?

00:23:09.020 --> 00:23:12.581
It was brief, but he definitely
communicated with them.

00:23:12.657 --> 00:23:14.716
Rentrillic trajectory.

00:23:14.793 --> 00:23:16.226
Unfortunately,
they never got around

00:23:16.294 --> 00:23:17.659
to explaining what that meant.

00:23:17.729 --> 00:23:19.458
Could be some sort
of alien geometry,

00:23:19.531 --> 00:23:21.396
but we'll need much more.

00:23:21.466 --> 00:23:24.367
Is it safe for him
to try to make contact again?

00:23:24.436 --> 00:23:26.336
Medically speaking, yes.

00:23:26.405 --> 00:23:28.532
The problem is convincing
the Commander of that.

00:23:34.646 --> 00:23:37.342
I realize you're frightened...

00:23:37.416 --> 00:23:41.284
but you're our only hope
out of this place.

00:23:41.353 --> 00:23:45.346
You think this
could risk your sanity.

00:23:45.424 --> 00:23:47.517
But your sanity
won't do you any good

00:23:47.592 --> 00:23:49.617
if we remain in chaotic space.

00:23:51.863 --> 00:23:54.388
I need you to keep
trying, Chakotay.

00:23:54.466 --> 00:23:56.263
Will you keep trying?

00:24:05.777 --> 00:24:07.176
Keep me posted.

00:24:09.848 --> 00:24:11.975
Are you ready to continue?

00:24:15.520 --> 00:24:19.047
Try to focus
on the alien voices.

00:24:19.124 --> 00:24:22.389
Tell me what they're saying.

00:24:22.461 --> 00:24:24.190
I can't hear them.

00:24:24.262 --> 00:24:25.524
Are you sure?

00:24:25.597 --> 00:24:27.155
Listen carefully.

00:24:34.206 --> 00:24:35.537
Maybe we can return you

00:24:35.607 --> 00:24:37.802
to a more receptive
frame of mind.

00:24:37.876 --> 00:24:39.935
Think back to when
you first heard them

00:24:40.078 --> 00:24:41.568
in the vision quest.

00:24:41.646 --> 00:24:43.079
What were you doing?

00:24:43.148 --> 00:24:44.615
Where were you?

00:24:46.151 --> 00:24:48.881
In a boxing ring.

00:24:48.954 --> 00:24:50.888
A strange ring.

00:24:50.956 --> 00:24:52.514
Was anyone else there?

00:24:54.059 --> 00:24:56.323
Yes.

00:24:56.394 --> 00:24:57.520
My opponent...

00:24:59.364 --> 00:25:00.626
Kid Chaos.

00:25:00.699 --> 00:25:02.030
Describe him.

00:25:10.942 --> 00:25:12.307
Tuvok...

00:25:12.377 --> 00:25:13.571
move into position.

00:25:14.946 --> 00:25:18.404
Thompson and Sharr,
target the midsection.

00:25:18.483 --> 00:25:20.542
Ensign MacAlister,
you and I will aim for the head.

00:25:20.619 --> 00:25:21.916
Set your phasers to kill.

00:25:22.020 --> 00:25:23.749
Not exactly

00:25:23.822 --> 00:25:25.915
the Marquis of Queensberry
rules, now, is it?

00:25:25.991 --> 00:25:27.288
"Set to kill"?

00:25:27.359 --> 00:25:28.656
That's not even Starfleet.

00:25:28.727 --> 00:25:30.388
Put down the weapons, son.

00:25:30.462 --> 00:25:32.930
Tactical advice from
an Academy groundskeeper?

00:25:33.064 --> 00:25:35.123
We fire at your command, sir.

00:25:35.200 --> 00:25:36.132
Give that order

00:25:36.201 --> 00:25:37.896
and you'll be
out for the count...

00:25:37.969 --> 00:25:38.936
the whole lot of you.

00:25:41.006 --> 00:25:42.166
Lower your weapons.

00:25:42.240 --> 00:25:43.502
Commander...

00:25:43.575 --> 00:25:45.167
I said stand down!

00:25:50.282 --> 00:25:53.342
We just heard from Vegas,
Mars and Orion III.

00:25:53.418 --> 00:25:55.784
The odds are running 33:1
that he'll outpoint you.

00:25:55.854 --> 00:25:57.754
11:1 that you'll be kayoed
by the fifth.

00:25:57.822 --> 00:26:01.349
Subspace radio is calling it
"The Disaster in the Delta."

00:26:01.426 --> 00:26:02.620
We can still scratch the card.

00:26:02.694 --> 00:26:03.626
I'll call the Doctor.

00:26:03.695 --> 00:26:05.026
We'll get you out on a medical.

00:26:05.096 --> 00:26:07.121
He's trying to hornswoggle us.

00:26:07.198 --> 00:26:09.029
Double-check those calculations.

00:26:09.100 --> 00:26:11.034
Let me see that padd.

00:26:11.102 --> 00:26:12.228
No. Fine.

00:26:12.304 --> 00:26:13.999
Don't want to trust
your friends?

00:26:14.072 --> 00:26:15.403
You're on your own.

00:26:30.288 --> 00:26:31.755
I'm filing a grievance

00:26:31.823 --> 00:26:34.451
with the Delta Quadrant
Boxing Commission!

00:26:34.526 --> 00:26:36.551
This bout came out of nowhere!

00:26:36.628 --> 00:26:37.925
There's some sort
of scheduling mix-up.

00:26:38.063 --> 00:26:39.553
You haven't had
the time to train.

00:26:39.631 --> 00:26:40.563
You're not ready!

00:26:40.632 --> 00:26:42.862
If you fight now,
you'll be destroyed!

00:26:43.935 --> 00:26:45.163
I can't fight now.

00:26:45.236 --> 00:26:46.533
I'm not ready for this.

00:26:46.605 --> 00:26:47.537
Come on!

00:26:47.606 --> 00:26:49.335
I can't stay here!

00:27:03.054 --> 00:27:06.217
I follow your example,
learn from you,

00:27:06.291 --> 00:27:07.417
look up to you.

00:27:07.492 --> 00:27:08.891
I don't want to lose that.

00:27:08.960 --> 00:27:10.791
You'll find another role model.

00:27:10.862 --> 00:27:12.056
You'll be okay.

00:27:12.130 --> 00:27:13.859
You're my First Officer.

00:27:13.932 --> 00:27:15.422
Your duty is to this crew.

00:27:15.500 --> 00:27:18.230
If something happens to me,
you've got to get Voyager home.

00:27:18.303 --> 00:27:20.999
Tuvok can take command.

00:27:23.074 --> 00:27:24.905
You're being selfish, Chakotay.

00:27:24.976 --> 00:27:27.945
I'm doing this for you...
for all of you!

00:27:31.883 --> 00:27:34.909
A delusion...
dementia puglistica.

00:27:34.986 --> 00:27:37.079
You're punch-drunk, Commander.

00:27:40.191 --> 00:27:42.159
A hard shot
to the head and neck,

00:27:42.227 --> 00:27:43.751
collapses the carotid artery

00:27:43.828 --> 00:27:45.796
and cuts the flow of blood
to the brain.

00:27:45.864 --> 00:27:48.298
The hook! The head and neck
twist laterally,

00:27:48.366 --> 00:27:50.334
traumatizing
the cerebral tissue.

00:27:50.402 --> 00:27:52.700
And who can forget
the upper cut?

00:27:52.771 --> 00:27:53.829
The head snaps back,

00:27:53.905 --> 00:27:55.770
rupturing tissue
in the cerebellum

00:27:55.840 --> 00:27:58.240
and upper spinal cord!

00:27:58.309 --> 00:27:59.936
Yes!

00:28:01.680 --> 00:28:03.113
And the result...

00:28:03.181 --> 00:28:06.776
of all this poetry in motion?

00:28:06.851 --> 00:28:08.580
Neurologic dysfunction,

00:28:08.653 --> 00:28:11.520
chronic traumatic
encephalopathy,

00:28:11.589 --> 00:28:14.217
loss of balance
and coordination,

00:28:14.292 --> 00:28:16.760
loss of memory.

00:28:16.828 --> 00:28:18.318
Starting to sound... familiar?

00:28:18.396 --> 00:28:19.727
Chakotay's fine.

00:28:19.798 --> 00:28:22.289
He just needs a little
conditioning, that's all.

00:28:22.367 --> 00:28:25.530
He needs to listen
to his doctor

00:28:25.603 --> 00:28:27.070
and not to his fantasies.

00:28:27.138 --> 00:28:29.868
Step into that arena

00:28:29.941 --> 00:28:33.138
and you'll become
what you most fear.

00:28:33.211 --> 00:28:34.610
What are you talking about?

00:28:34.679 --> 00:28:36.909
Oh, he knows what I mean.

00:28:37.015 --> 00:28:38.846
Don't you, Chakotay?

00:28:38.917 --> 00:28:40.077
Hmm?

00:28:40.151 --> 00:28:42.051
What's wrong?

00:28:42.120 --> 00:28:43.485
Victory...

00:28:43.555 --> 00:28:45.921
defeat, knockout,

00:28:46.057 --> 00:28:47.319
TKO...

00:28:47.392 --> 00:28:48.791
it's all beside the point.

00:28:48.860 --> 00:28:51.328
We know how it really ends...

00:28:51.396 --> 00:28:54.923
"a crazy old man..."

00:28:55.033 --> 00:28:56.967
Hmm?

00:28:59.838 --> 00:29:02.602
It's your fate, your destiny.

00:29:02.674 --> 00:29:04.164
There's no escape.

00:29:04.242 --> 00:29:05.971
You've just got to do your best.

00:29:06.044 --> 00:29:08.672
You can't let yourself
give in to your fears.

00:29:08.747 --> 00:29:10.044
I'm not afraid!

00:29:10.115 --> 00:29:12.481
Who said you were?

00:29:23.762 --> 00:29:25.457
I'm sorry!

00:29:28.166 --> 00:29:30.134
Please come back.

00:29:38.243 --> 00:29:40.643
They got away.

00:29:40.712 --> 00:29:42.202
Grandfather.

00:29:42.280 --> 00:29:43.907
Where did you go?

00:29:44.015 --> 00:29:46.381
Some people
were shouting at me.

00:29:46.451 --> 00:29:48.112
They were going for a walk

00:29:48.186 --> 00:29:51.553
and they wanted me
to come along.

00:29:51.623 --> 00:29:52.715
Oh...

00:29:52.791 --> 00:29:54.918
It's hard to follow them.

00:29:54.993 --> 00:29:59.521
Oh, God, they go
to strange places.

00:29:59.597 --> 00:30:01.326
I'm supposed to be watching you.

00:30:01.399 --> 00:30:03.697
We're going to get in trouble
if we don't go back home.

00:30:05.737 --> 00:30:07.466
Be a good boy and go.

00:30:07.539 --> 00:30:08.938
We understand.

00:30:09.073 --> 00:30:11.541
You have to come with me.

00:30:13.711 --> 00:30:16.680
They say you can come with us.

00:30:18.483 --> 00:30:20.314
There's nobody else here.

00:30:20.385 --> 00:30:24.287
They say you're
just like we are.

00:30:24.355 --> 00:30:25.287
I'm not!

00:30:25.356 --> 00:30:27.324
I'm not like you.

00:30:30.728 --> 00:30:32.958
It's not so bad.

00:30:33.031 --> 00:30:36.489
When you get used to it,
they're not so bad.

00:30:38.436 --> 00:30:40.904
They're just a lot of talk.

00:30:40.972 --> 00:30:44.135
Sometimes I wish
they were more quiet.

00:30:44.209 --> 00:30:46.404
But they like to talk.

00:30:52.116 --> 00:30:54.676
Come home.

00:30:54.752 --> 00:30:56.652
No.

00:30:56.721 --> 00:30:58.279
I'm too tired.

00:31:00.391 --> 00:31:03.849
This is a nice place...

00:31:03.928 --> 00:31:07.420
a nice place to call home.

00:31:07.498 --> 00:31:08.863
Hmm.

00:31:16.007 --> 00:31:18.669
Begin Round One.

00:31:18.743 --> 00:31:21.143
Did you hear that?

00:31:21.212 --> 00:31:22.236
No.

00:31:22.313 --> 00:31:23.803
Yes, you did.

00:31:27.719 --> 00:31:30.552
There's a lot of them this time.

00:31:30.622 --> 00:31:32.249
Tell them to go away!

00:31:32.323 --> 00:31:33.756
Go away!

00:31:35.760 --> 00:31:38.194
They've got other ideas.

00:31:40.164 --> 00:31:42.291
I have to go home!

00:31:42.367 --> 00:31:45.234
Wait. They're coming for you.

00:31:45.303 --> 00:31:49.069
The challenger... Chakotay!

00:31:50.675 --> 00:31:51.733
Better late than never.

00:31:51.809 --> 00:31:53.299
They almost scrubbed the bout.

00:31:53.378 --> 00:31:54.310
I'm afraid.

00:31:54.379 --> 00:31:55.539
I know you are.

00:31:55.613 --> 00:31:57.979
You'd be a liar if you
said anything else.

00:31:58.049 --> 00:31:59.482
But I've always been afraid.

00:31:59.550 --> 00:32:01.142
I know that, too.

00:32:01.219 --> 00:32:04.985
The champion... Kid Chaos!

00:32:09.894 --> 00:32:11.293
That's it!

00:32:11.362 --> 00:32:13.330
All over!

00:32:13.398 --> 00:32:16.856
The fight's been canceled
on medical grounds!

00:32:18.970 --> 00:32:20.494
Put 'em down. Let's go.

00:32:20.571 --> 00:32:23.938
I hear there's some bearbaiting
at the arena next door!

00:32:24.075 --> 00:32:25.201
Have fun!

00:32:30.782 --> 00:32:32.215
He's coming out of it.

00:32:35.219 --> 00:32:37.380
You stopped the fight.

00:32:37.455 --> 00:32:39.218
You were stuck
in the vision quest.

00:32:39.290 --> 00:32:40.257
I've got to go back.

00:32:40.325 --> 00:32:41.587
You're going nowhere
but Sick Bay.

00:32:41.659 --> 00:32:42.626
Let me go.

00:32:42.694 --> 00:32:44.286
Calm down.
It's over for you.

00:32:44.362 --> 00:32:45.954
- No, let me get in the ring!
- Chakotay...

00:32:46.030 --> 00:32:48.123
No. Let me back in the ring.
Let me...

00:33:07.752 --> 00:33:09.447
200,000 kilometers.

00:33:09.520 --> 00:33:11.579
Launch another beacon.

00:33:11.656 --> 00:33:13.283
Beacon launched.

00:33:13.358 --> 00:33:16.486
I'm reading a shift
of.003 in the graviton shear.

00:33:16.561 --> 00:33:17.493
Status?

00:33:17.562 --> 00:33:18.927
Shields holding.

00:33:19.030 --> 00:33:21.328
Speed is steady
at one-quarter impulse.

00:33:21.399 --> 00:33:23.924
Maintain course
and heading, Mr. Paris.

00:33:25.470 --> 00:33:27.438
Sensors are functioning.

00:33:27.505 --> 00:33:29.769
Our course is still clear.

00:33:29.841 --> 00:33:33.538
Captain, I recommend we go
to three-quarters impulse.

00:33:33.611 --> 00:33:36.239
Increasing power to the engines
could affect chaotic space.

00:33:36.314 --> 00:33:38.578
There are too many unknowns.

00:33:38.649 --> 00:33:41.743
At this speed, we should see
daylight in about two months.

00:33:41.819 --> 00:33:43.878
The longer we're
in chaotic space, the longer

00:33:43.955 --> 00:33:45.786
we're exposed
to these unknowns.

00:33:45.857 --> 00:33:47.882
His logic is undeniable,
Captain.

00:33:47.959 --> 00:33:49.392
We should increase our speed.

00:33:49.460 --> 00:33:51.052
Finally.

00:33:51.129 --> 00:33:53.893
Who am I to dispute logic?

00:33:53.965 --> 00:33:55.330
Take a look at this.

00:33:58.369 --> 00:34:01.497
It's the first beacon
we launched three hours ago.

00:34:02.974 --> 00:34:05.169
We've been going in circles?

00:34:05.243 --> 00:34:08.804
To be precise, one large circle.

00:34:08.880 --> 00:34:10.939
Hold our position.

00:34:13.951 --> 00:34:16.579
All stop.

00:34:17.922 --> 00:34:18.911
Report.

00:34:19.057 --> 00:34:20.922
I've applied 10,053 algorithms

00:34:21.059 --> 00:34:23.823
to the energy signatures
produced by chaotic space.

00:34:23.895 --> 00:34:26.227
There is a pattern.

00:34:26.297 --> 00:34:28.595
Order to chaos?

00:34:28.666 --> 00:34:30.429
Observe.

00:34:30.501 --> 00:34:32.264
An isolinear frequency.

00:34:32.336 --> 00:34:33.894
Some kind of signal?

00:34:33.971 --> 00:34:36.166
I haven't located the source.

00:34:36.240 --> 00:34:38.401
It may be natural...
a star or quasar

00:34:38.476 --> 00:34:41.274
that has managed to survive
in chaotic space.

00:34:41.345 --> 00:34:44.337
But it could be a transmission.

00:34:44.415 --> 00:34:45.848
Possibly.

00:34:45.917 --> 00:34:46.849
Have you tried

00:34:46.918 --> 00:34:48.852
the standard language
decryptions?

00:34:48.920 --> 00:34:50.512
All of them with no success.

00:34:50.588 --> 00:34:53.887
Success seems to be
in short supply lately.

00:35:01.566 --> 00:35:03.727
Impossible.

00:35:03.801 --> 00:35:04.768
Captain?

00:35:06.537 --> 00:35:09.131
And to think...

00:35:09.207 --> 00:35:12.199
that kept me
from getting an "A."

00:35:12.276 --> 00:35:13.903
It was the only question
I missed

00:35:14.045 --> 00:35:15.672
in exo-genetics my senior year.

00:35:15.746 --> 00:35:17.543
The nucleotide
resonance frequency.

00:35:17.615 --> 00:35:19.776
That signal was designed
to activate DNA.

00:35:19.851 --> 00:35:21.580
It realigned
his molecular bonds.

00:35:21.652 --> 00:35:22.914
Now do you believe me?

00:35:22.987 --> 00:35:25.217
They're the ones
who scheduled the fight.

00:35:25.289 --> 00:35:26.221
They're promoting it.

00:35:26.290 --> 00:35:27.587
They're putting up the purse.

00:35:27.658 --> 00:35:29.182
His sensory cortex
is hyperactive.

00:35:29.260 --> 00:35:30.386
He's still hallucinating.

00:35:30.461 --> 00:35:31.928
It's not an hallucination

00:35:31.996 --> 00:35:33.930
not a vision quest...
it's a prizefight!

00:35:34.031 --> 00:35:35.498
Chakotay, do you know me?

00:35:35.566 --> 00:35:36.897
Do you know where you are?

00:35:36.968 --> 00:35:38.162
I know you, Captain,

00:35:38.236 --> 00:35:39.498
but you stopped the fight.

00:35:39.570 --> 00:35:40.696
You ruined my career!

00:35:40.771 --> 00:35:42.500
Nobody is going to put me
on the card after this!

00:35:42.573 --> 00:35:43.904
It's better for you
to rest, Chakotay,

00:35:43.975 --> 00:35:45.943
until we can figure out
why this is happening to you.

00:35:46.043 --> 00:35:47.567
They want to contact me.

00:35:47.645 --> 00:35:48.634
Who does?

00:35:48.713 --> 00:35:50.271
The people who live here.

00:35:50.348 --> 00:35:51.542
This will sedate him.

00:35:51.616 --> 00:35:52.776
Wait a minute.

00:35:52.850 --> 00:35:55.444
You believe somebody
lives here, in chaotic space?

00:35:55.520 --> 00:35:57.750
And they're trying
to communicate with you?

00:35:57.822 --> 00:35:59.915
Yes! I saw him!

00:35:59.991 --> 00:36:01.219
Tell me about him.

00:36:01.292 --> 00:36:02.759
What does he look like?

00:36:02.827 --> 00:36:04.385
He's got a couple
of kilos on me,

00:36:04.462 --> 00:36:05.724
a few centimeters in height,

00:36:05.796 --> 00:36:07.127
but I can take him, Captain!

00:36:07.198 --> 00:36:10.565
I just have to stay
off the ropes.

00:36:10.635 --> 00:36:14.503
The holodeck boxing simulation
is still strong in his memory.

00:36:14.572 --> 00:36:16.699
Obviously, it's the primary
source of imagery

00:36:16.774 --> 00:36:18.435
for his hallucinations.

00:36:18.509 --> 00:36:22.912
What if those hallucinations
are being induced for a purpose?

00:36:22.980 --> 00:36:26.381
Aliens who exist
on some perceptual wavelength

00:36:26.450 --> 00:36:28.611
that our senses can't detect

00:36:28.686 --> 00:36:31.621
and the only way for them
to communicate

00:36:31.689 --> 00:36:34.624
with us is to alter our senses.

00:36:34.692 --> 00:36:37.058
Chakotay's bad gene
gave them the opportunity.

00:36:37.128 --> 00:36:38.686
What are you proposing?

00:36:38.763 --> 00:36:41.129
Remember the derelict ship?

00:36:41.199 --> 00:36:44.532
Two of their crew members
claimed they were seeing things.

00:36:44.602 --> 00:36:47.298
Was somebody trying
to communicate with them?

00:36:47.371 --> 00:36:49.464
Was somebody trying
to warn them, help them?

00:36:49.540 --> 00:36:50.507
Or trying to destroy them,

00:36:50.575 --> 00:36:51.940
just as they're trying
to destroy us.

00:36:52.076 --> 00:36:53.134
Why go through all the trouble?

00:36:53.211 --> 00:36:54.143
We're trapped here anyway.

00:36:54.212 --> 00:36:57.181
Let me back in the ring!

00:36:57.248 --> 00:36:58.545
Even if this is

00:36:58.616 --> 00:37:00.311
some kind
of alien communication,

00:37:00.384 --> 00:37:02.011
it could harm him permanently.

00:37:02.086 --> 00:37:03.781
Bridge to Captain Janeway.

00:37:03.854 --> 00:37:04.878
Go ahead, Tuvok.

00:37:04.989 --> 00:37:06.786
Graviton shear
has increased again.

00:37:06.857 --> 00:37:08.085
Hull pressure is rising.

00:37:08.159 --> 00:37:09.421
I'm on my way.

00:37:09.493 --> 00:37:10.892
Captain...

00:37:11.028 --> 00:37:15.590
when have we ever turned away
from a first contact?

00:37:21.038 --> 00:37:23.506
Send him back in the ring.

00:37:33.985 --> 00:37:35.111
Report!

00:37:35.186 --> 00:37:37.450
Some kind of spatial sinkhole
just opened up beneath us!

00:37:37.521 --> 00:37:38.954
Full thrusters!

00:37:42.827 --> 00:37:43.759
Status?

00:37:43.828 --> 00:37:45.591
We managed to sidestep that one,

00:37:45.663 --> 00:37:49.224
but graviton shear has increased
by another 310 percent.

00:37:49.300 --> 00:37:50.289
Janeway to Sick Bay.

00:37:50.368 --> 00:37:51.300
Sick Bay here.

00:37:51.369 --> 00:37:52.700
It's now or never.

00:37:52.770 --> 00:37:53.862
Understood, Captain.

00:37:53.938 --> 00:37:55.337
I've got to get in there.

00:37:55.406 --> 00:37:57.203
They're about to ring the bell.

00:37:57.275 --> 00:37:59.175
I'm going to subject
you to a field

00:37:59.243 --> 00:38:01.370
that will enhance
the nucleotide bonds.

00:38:01.445 --> 00:38:04.710
The gene should become
fully activated.

00:38:04.782 --> 00:38:05.874
Do you understand?

00:38:05.950 --> 00:38:08.384
I understand.

00:38:08.452 --> 00:38:10.545
Find us a way out of here.

00:38:10.621 --> 00:38:11.849
I'll try.

00:38:29.440 --> 00:38:30.407
Good idea.

00:38:30.474 --> 00:38:31.566
Keep him waiting.

00:38:31.642 --> 00:38:33.337
Let him sweat it out.

00:38:33.411 --> 00:38:35.777
In this corner, representing

00:38:35.846 --> 00:38:38.246
the Alpha Quadrant,
Earth and humanity,

00:38:38.316 --> 00:38:40.580
the challenger, Chakotay!

00:38:42.853 --> 00:38:45.048
Everybody loves an underdog.

00:38:47.024 --> 00:38:48.889
And in this corner,

00:38:48.959 --> 00:38:52.793
champion of the Delta Quadrant,
Kid Chaos!

00:38:54.865 --> 00:38:56.127
Looks like he's got

00:38:56.200 --> 00:38:58.293
a lot of upper-body
strength... a real puncher.

00:38:58.369 --> 00:39:00.496
Just keep your elbow low
when you throw the right

00:39:00.571 --> 00:39:02.630
and don't come in too straight;
you'll be okay.

00:39:02.707 --> 00:39:04.140
Where's the scouting report?

00:39:04.208 --> 00:39:05.470
We don't know anything
about this guy.

00:39:05.543 --> 00:39:07.204
I don't know who I'm up against!

00:39:07.278 --> 00:39:08.711
You're up against yourself.

00:39:08.779 --> 00:39:10.872
That's all
you've got to remember

00:39:10.948 --> 00:39:13.542
and don't raise the elbow.

00:39:13.617 --> 00:39:15.414
Begin Round One.

00:39:27.898 --> 00:39:29.889
Boothby, where are you?

00:39:29.967 --> 00:39:31.127
Still here, son.

00:39:31.202 --> 00:39:32.635
I'm not going anywhere.

00:39:44.582 --> 00:39:45.446
You... Are...

00:39:45.516 --> 00:39:46.005
Far from where...

00:39:46.083 --> 00:39:47.573
You... Call home.

00:39:48.686 --> 00:39:50.586
You... Are... Lost.

00:39:50.654 --> 00:39:52.144
Do you understand?

00:39:52.223 --> 00:39:53.918
Yes.

00:39:53.991 --> 00:39:56.926
We are far from home.

00:39:56.994 --> 00:39:58.928
We are lost.

00:39:59.063 --> 00:39:59.791
- Our...
- Home...

00:39:59.864 --> 00:40:00.592
Is here.

00:40:01.399 --> 00:40:02.923
Our... Home... Is here...

00:40:03.734 --> 00:40:04.928
In chaotic space.

00:40:05.002 --> 00:40:07.061
- Chaotic space...
- Chaotic space...

00:40:07.138 --> 00:40:08.799
Hang in there, son.

00:40:08.873 --> 00:40:09.805
Protect your head!

00:40:09.874 --> 00:40:10.932
I understand!

00:40:11.075 --> 00:40:12.201
- We are too...
- Alien...

00:40:12.276 --> 00:40:13.641
- For you.
- We are too...

00:40:13.711 --> 00:40:14.871
- Strange...
- For you.

00:40:14.945 --> 00:40:16.503
Maybe we're the ones

00:40:16.580 --> 00:40:19.777
who are too alien...
too strange.

00:40:19.850 --> 00:40:20.714
- Lf...
- You...

00:40:20.785 --> 00:40:22.480
- Stay...
- In chaotic space...

00:40:22.553 --> 00:40:24.180
- Chaotic space...
- Chaotic space...

00:40:24.255 --> 00:40:25.813
You'll be destroyed!

00:40:25.890 --> 00:40:26.948
We know that...

00:40:27.024 --> 00:40:28.958
but we can't navigate.

00:40:29.059 --> 00:40:31.960
Our sensors don't work
in your space.

00:40:32.096 --> 00:40:34.291
20 more seconds!
Don't go down!

00:40:35.599 --> 00:40:36.623
- Your...
- Sensors must be...

00:40:36.700 --> 00:40:38.190
Realigned...

00:40:38.269 --> 00:40:39.566
How can I?

00:40:39.637 --> 00:40:40.569
- Your mind...
- Must be...

00:40:40.638 --> 00:40:41.696
- Realigned...
- Realigned...

00:40:41.772 --> 00:40:42.796
Realigned.

00:40:42.873 --> 00:40:43.805
- Your mind...
- Must be...

00:40:43.874 --> 00:40:46.138
- Realigned.
- I understand.

00:40:46.210 --> 00:40:47.871
End Round One.

00:40:47.945 --> 00:40:48.877
Get them out!

00:40:48.946 --> 00:40:49.878
Let go, Commander!

00:40:49.947 --> 00:40:51.574
I can't take any more punches!

00:40:51.649 --> 00:40:53.082
They aren't hitting you.

00:40:53.150 --> 00:40:54.447
Duck... feint...

00:40:54.518 --> 00:40:55.450
clinch!

00:40:55.519 --> 00:40:56.451
Stop fighting!

00:40:56.520 --> 00:40:57.487
I can't!
They'll destroy me!

00:40:57.555 --> 00:40:58.647
That's a risk
you'll have to take.

00:40:58.722 --> 00:40:59.654
You take the damn risk!

00:40:59.723 --> 00:41:00.655
They want you.

00:41:00.724 --> 00:41:01.656
Why?

00:41:01.725 --> 00:41:03.192
Because you have the gene.

00:41:03.260 --> 00:41:04.386
The crazy gene.

00:41:04.462 --> 00:41:06.157
Yes, the crazy gene.

00:41:06.230 --> 00:41:08.061
The aliens are trying

00:41:08.132 --> 00:41:09.258
to speak to you,
and the only thing

00:41:09.333 --> 00:41:10.459
keeping you
from understanding them

00:41:10.534 --> 00:41:12.866
is your own fear...
your fear of losing control,

00:41:12.937 --> 00:41:14.234
your fear of the unknown...

00:41:14.305 --> 00:41:16.865
The unknown and I
don't want to know.

00:41:16.941 --> 00:41:19.933
But we have to know
or we're all going to die.

00:41:20.010 --> 00:41:23.036
Allow yourself to hear them
for just a few moments.

00:41:23.113 --> 00:41:24.205
Do it for us.

00:41:24.281 --> 00:41:27.182
What will happen to me...
when they're done?

00:41:27.251 --> 00:41:28.775
You'll be on Voyager...

00:41:28.853 --> 00:41:30.718
surrounded by friends.

00:41:30.788 --> 00:41:32.119
I can't understand them.

00:41:32.189 --> 00:41:33.281
You will.

00:41:33.357 --> 00:41:35.154
They're talking too
fast, too many words.

00:41:35.226 --> 00:41:36.784
Try to focus
on one word at a time.

00:41:36.861 --> 00:41:37.793
Too many words.

00:41:37.862 --> 00:41:38.794
- Don't stop.
- I'm scared.

00:41:38.863 --> 00:41:40.387
- Let them in.
- I don't want to die!

00:41:40.464 --> 00:41:42.455
They won't hurt you!
No one will hurt you!

00:41:44.368 --> 00:41:46.962
18th gradient,
trimetric fracture.

00:41:47.037 --> 00:41:47.969
Keep going.

00:41:48.038 --> 00:41:49.733
We have to modify
our deflector.

00:41:49.807 --> 00:41:52.742
We have to induce a paralateral
rentrillic trajectory.

00:41:52.810 --> 00:41:54.072
How do we do that?

00:41:54.144 --> 00:41:55.406
I think I understand.

00:41:55.479 --> 00:41:57.413
It's making sense.

00:41:57.481 --> 00:41:58.573
Where are you going?

00:41:58.649 --> 00:42:00.412
I can make
the adjustments myself.

00:42:00.484 --> 00:42:02.076
I have to get to the Bridge.

00:42:02.152 --> 00:42:05.280
I don't know how much longer
I can keep it in my mind!

00:42:07.458 --> 00:42:08.823
- Commander.
- What happened?

00:42:08.893 --> 00:42:10.485
He's got a right uppercut
that almost knocked me out.

00:42:10.561 --> 00:42:11.493
Move over, Harry.

00:42:11.562 --> 00:42:12.494
Hang on, Ensign.

00:42:12.563 --> 00:42:13.791
They showed me
how to get out of here.

00:42:13.864 --> 00:42:14.796
He's hallucinating.

00:42:14.865 --> 00:42:15.797
Out of the way!

00:42:15.866 --> 00:42:16.798
Tell us what to do.

00:42:16.867 --> 00:42:18.494
I can't! It's too
difficult to explain.

00:42:18.569 --> 00:42:20.127
I'm locking him out.

00:42:20.204 --> 00:42:20.932
No.

00:42:21.005 --> 00:42:22.632
Give up your post.

00:42:23.674 --> 00:42:26.165
He's recalibrating
the deflector dish

00:42:26.243 --> 00:42:28.404
and routing it
through the sensor array.

00:42:28.479 --> 00:42:31.346
It must be altered.

00:42:31.415 --> 00:42:34.179
Captain, the graviton shear
is increasing.

00:42:34.251 --> 00:42:36.151
I'm reading microfractures
on the hull.

00:42:36.220 --> 00:42:38.450
Stay and we'll be destroyed.

00:42:38.522 --> 00:42:40.888
Activate the deflector...
maximum amplitude.

00:42:40.958 --> 00:42:42.687
Bring sensors on line.

00:42:42.760 --> 00:42:43.419
Captain...

00:42:43.494 --> 00:42:44.483
Do it.

00:42:49.733 --> 00:42:50.961
I don't know how,

00:42:51.068 --> 00:42:53.093
but the sensors have
found us a course.

00:42:53.170 --> 00:42:55.764
Maximum impulse... now!

00:42:55.839 --> 00:42:58.808
Captain,
if that course is wrong,

00:42:58.876 --> 00:43:00.901
we could breech our hull.

00:43:00.978 --> 00:43:02.275
Engage.

00:43:19.163 --> 00:43:21.063
We've reentered normal space.

00:43:22.466 --> 00:43:25.594
Mr. Paris, resume a course
to the Alpha Quadrant.

00:43:25.669 --> 00:43:27.637
Aye, sir.

00:43:45.723 --> 00:43:47.190
When I said you should take

00:43:47.257 --> 00:43:49.452
the next day or two off,
I thought you'd want to stay

00:43:49.526 --> 00:43:50.686
in your quarters
with a good book.

00:43:50.761 --> 00:43:52.456
Boxing helps me unwind.

00:43:52.529 --> 00:43:53.962
Well, in that case,
report for duty

00:43:54.098 --> 00:43:55.224
first thing in the morning.

00:43:55.299 --> 00:43:56.493
See you then.

00:43:58.702 --> 00:44:02.798
Computer, run Chakotay
Training Program 15-Beta.

00:44:22.993 --> 00:44:25.393
Ah, come for a little
more punishment?

00:44:25.462 --> 00:44:27.589
Thought I'd spar
for a few rounds.

00:44:27.665 --> 00:44:29.565
Uh-huh, after that last bout?

00:44:29.633 --> 00:44:31.601
Did you talk to the Doc?

00:44:31.669 --> 00:44:33.603
I've got a clean bill
of health.

00:44:33.671 --> 00:44:35.229
That's good enough for me.

00:44:35.305 --> 00:44:37.102
Okay.

00:44:37.174 --> 00:44:38.937
I've been watching him fight.

00:44:39.009 --> 00:44:41.603
He falls in too much
when he clinches

00:44:41.679 --> 00:44:44.773
and he moves more to his right
than he does to his left.

00:44:44.848 --> 00:44:46.941
Well, I'll double up
on the left jabs

00:44:47.017 --> 00:44:48.211
and see what happens.

00:44:48.285 --> 00:44:50.150
You sure
you're ready for this?

00:44:51.955 --> 00:44:53.650
I'm ready.

00:44:53.724 --> 00:44:54.691
Okay.

00:44:55.959 --> 00:44:57.927
Begin Round One.
